1
00:01:40,674 --> 00:01:44,216
向你致意!
Salutations!

2
00:01:44,757 --> 00:01:46,674
RWBY小队 早上好呀!
Good morning, team RWBY!

3
00:01:46,924 --> 00:01:48,049
呃 Penny
Ugh, Penny.

4
00:01:48,091 --> 00:01:49,799
现在才什么时间?
What time is it even?

5
00:01:49,841 --> 00:01:52,424
当然是猎人时间啦!
Time to be Huntresses, of course!

6
00:01:53,966 --> 00:01:56,882
耶!
Yahoo!

7
00:02:02,591 --> 00:02:04,341
好吧 拿去吧
Sure, take it.

8
00:02:05,049 --> 00:02:06,257
猎人们 看这里
Eyes up, Huntsmen.

9
00:02:06,591 --> 00:02:08,882
是时候适应擎天的新日常了
Time to get used to the new normal in Atlas.

10
00:02:11,382 --> 00:02:14,382
你们的最优先的任务是阿米特通讯塔
Your top priority is Amity Tower.

11
00:02:14,424 --> 00:02:17,716
这就意味着你们必须从戮兽和土匪手中保护物资
That means protecting supply runs from Grimm and bandits.

12
00:02:18,299 --> 00:02:20,257
同时也要保护基地自身
And, protecting the site itself.

13
00:02:22,841 --> 00:02:25,924
将所有资源转移到阿米特通讯塔工程意味着
Diverting all construction resources to Amity Tower means

14
00:02:25,966 --> 00:02:29,424
曼特城对戮兽的防御将变得薄弱
there are going to be gaps in Mantle's defenses against Grimm.

15
00:02:29,674 --> 00:02:31,757
它的周边防御会需要你们的帮助
They'll need help on the perimeter.

16
00:02:35,007 --> 00:02:38,091
嘿 你们两个有没有想过拓展一下技巧?
Hey, have you two ever thought about branching out a little?

17
00:02:38,132 --> 00:02:40,966
你们总是成对战斗 但我不知道你们的风格是不是..
You always pair up, but I don't know if your styles really-

18
00:02:52,549 --> 00:02:55,257
挺... 挺好的!
Really, really good stuff!

19
00:02:55,799 --> 00:02:56,924
加油 继续保持!
Yeah, keep it up!

20
00:02:57,049 --> 00:02:58,716
排成一队走 就像之前练习那样
Single file line, you know the drill.

21
00:02:58,882 --> 00:03:00,882
然而在曼特城中 也有很多要做的事
But there's still plenty to do in Mantle itself.

22
00:03:01,966 --> 00:03:04,466
噢 又一份砂锅菜 不必了吧
Oh, another casserole, that's too kind.

23
00:03:04,507 --> 00:03:07,257
我想你们会意识到 大家乐于看到身边有猎人守护
I think you'll find everyone appreciates having a Huntsman around.

24
00:03:07,299 --> 00:03:08,799
换个发型就成方人迷了
It's totally the haircut.

25
00:03:10,091 --> 00:03:13,382
如果你们觉得合适 你们就可以享受假期
You're of course free to enjoy your time off as you see fit.

26
00:03:14,174 --> 00:03:16,091
只要能让你们有所进步
Whatever helps you take the edge off.

27
00:03:21,257 --> 00:03:23,341
奥斯卡 你可能再也没有听到奥兹的声音了
You might not hear Oz anymore, Oscar

28
00:03:23,382 --> 00:03:25,466
但这不意味着我们不能把他逼出来
but that doesn't mean we can't try to jog him loose.

29
00:03:26,132 --> 00:03:27,466
你有什么想法?
What did you have in mind?

30
00:03:30,716 --> 00:03:33,507
你们身边的猎人就是无价的财富
The Huntsmen around you can be an invaluable resource.

31
00:03:33,966 --> 00:03:35,591
只要你们愿意去留意的话
If you're willing to pay attention.

32
00:03:41,716 --> 00:03:44,216
你有想过延展你的元气吗?
Have you ever thought about extending your aura?

33
00:03:44,757 --> 00:03:47,716
但是不要担心 这里已经不是学校了
But make no mistake, school's over.

34
00:03:48,466 --> 00:03:51,674
你可以自由选择想要成为哪种猎人
You get to choose what type of Huntsman, or Huntress you are.

35
00:03:56,966 --> 00:03:57,841
再来
Again.

36
00:04:01,174 --> 00:04:03,466
Penny Penny!
Penny, Penny!

37
00:04:03,841 --> 00:04:05,716
昨天我和Weiss呃呃呃.
So yesterday Weiss and I were like

38
00:04:05,882 --> 00:04:07,132
然后它们就啊啊啊..
and they were like-

39
00:04:10,966 --> 00:04:13,424
所以 以后会怎么样呢?
So, what's it gonna be?

40
00:04:18,132 --> 00:04:19,757
不要踩错拍子 不要踩错拍子
Never miss a beat, never miss a beat.

41
00:04:19,966 --> 00:04:20,757
借过!
Excuse me!

42
00:04:24,466 --> 00:04:25,257
快来小闪电
Come on, lightning bolt,

43
00:04:25,299 --> 00:04:27,257
你不是很快的吗?
aren't you supposed to be fast?

44
00:04:29,216 --> 00:04:32,216
哇 你男朋友还挺能扛的
Wow, your boyfriend's actually holding his own!

45
00:04:32,591 --> 00:04:34,924
他和你在一起时的能量现在去哪儿了?
Where's all that energy when he's around you?

46
00:05:03,966 --> 00:05:05,174
哇!
Wow!

47
00:05:05,216 --> 00:05:07,174
太惊人了!
That was amazing!

48
00:05:07,799 --> 00:05:10,632
你们从维特锦标赛以来进步了好多
You guys have really improved since the Vytal Tournament,

49
00:05:10,674 --> 00:05:14,674
还有那个可爱的农场男孩 给了我们不少惊喜哦
And that cute farm boy had a few surprises for us, too.

50
00:05:16,799 --> 00:05:19,549
好吧 你们也有点让我们措手不及
Well, you really had us on our toes.

51
00:05:20,049 --> 00:05:21,674
有那么一会儿我都觉得要输了
Thought you had a there for a second, whew!

52
00:05:21,882 --> 00:05:24,841
瞎说 明明远不止一会儿的!
Oh c'mon, it was way more than a second!

53
00:05:25,382 --> 00:05:26,216
你们忙吗?
You guys busy?

54
00:05:26,507 --> 00:05:27,507
想吃午饭吗?
Wanna grab some lunch?

55
00:05:27,549 --> 00:05:28,382
我们?
Do we?

56
00:05:28,424 --> 00:05:30,382
我可以吃掉像考伯特这么大的三明治!
I could eat a sandwich the size of Kobalt!

57
00:05:34,757 --> 00:05:35,757
哦 不
Ah, man.

58
00:05:36,132 --> 00:05:37,507
我们很乐意 但是.
We'd love to, but...

59
00:05:37,549 --> 00:05:38,257
有任务了
Duty calls.

60
00:05:38,299 --> 00:05:39,466
或许下次?
Maybe some other time?

61
00:05:39,549 --> 00:05:40,424
没事!
No worries!

62
00:05:40,466 --> 00:05:42,424
等下次你们有空了再和我们说
The next time you're free, just let us know

63
00:05:42,466 --> 00:05:44,424
好 那就下次吧
Yeah, next time.

64
00:05:45,591 --> 00:05:47,174
嘿艾弗里 你要是点冻酸奶的话 能让我咬一口吗?
Hey Ivori, if you're gonna go get froyo, can I have a bite?

65
00:05:47,882 --> 00:05:48,757
你又来了!
Aw, come on!

66
00:05:49,049 --> 00:05:51,841
其实还是有吃三明治的时间对吧?
There's still time for sandwiches, right?

67
00:05:54,841 --> 00:05:58,632
不是我觉得无聊 但为什么我们不能用飞艇
Not that I'm bored, but why can't we just use

68
00:05:58,674 --> 00:06:00,632
把这些物资送到阿米特去?
an airship to take these supplies to Amity?

69
00:06:01,132 --> 00:06:04,632
这些用于通讯塔的组件太重了
The components for Amity Tower's construction are far too heavy.

70
00:06:04,882 --> 00:06:06,966
运输这些部件所消耗的贵重的尘晶
All that weight would require precious dust

71
00:06:07,007 --> 00:06:08,507
应该省下来为发射做准备
we should be saving for the launch itself.

72
00:06:08,882 --> 00:06:10,924
以及对付闻风而来的戮兽
that

73
00:06:11,757 --> 00:06:17,924
但这样的话 运输路程就会很长... 很长...
It just makes for long, very long, supply runs.

74
00:06:17,966 --> 00:06:20,174
至少苔原还是风景优美的
At least the tundra is scenic.

75
00:06:22,799 --> 00:06:23,507
确实
Totally.

76
00:06:30,049 --> 00:06:33,549
Ruby 我想告诉你 能够以专业的身份
Ruby, I just wanted to say how excited I am

77
00:06:33,591 --> 00:06:36,424
和你一起工作 我特别兴奋!
to be working with you in a professional capacity!

78
00:06:36,466 --> 00:06:37,466
作为朋友也一样
As friends!

79
00:06:39,341 --> 00:06:40,299
我也是 Penny
Me too, Penny.

80
00:06:40,966 --> 00:06:44,341
关系是如此有趣又多样!
Relationships are so interesting, and varied!

81
00:06:45,132 --> 00:06:47,049
说到朋友...
Speaking of friends...

82
00:06:47,424 --> 00:06:49,841
你有交新朋友吗?
Have you been able to make any new ones?

83
00:06:49,882 --> 00:06:51,799
从.. .你懂的?
Since, you know..?

84
00:06:52,174 --> 00:06:54,091
现在我是曼特城的正式守护者
Now that I'm the official Protector of Mantle

85
00:06:54,132 --> 00:06:55,716
我已经不需要一支队伍了
I don't really have a team anymore.

86
00:06:55,924 --> 00:06:58,674
埃隆伍德将军说我没时间交朋友
General Ironwood says! don't have time for friends

87
00:06:59,049 --> 00:07:03,424
哦 呃 你怎么觉得的?
Oh, uh, how do you feel about that?

88
00:07:04,216 --> 00:07:05,924
其实我希望自己能去做
I feel like I wish I could do

89
00:07:05,966 --> 00:07:09,507
所有我需要的和我想要的事情
both the things I need to do, and the things I want to do.

90
00:07:09,966 --> 00:07:11,049
这正常吗?
Is that normal?

91
00:07:12,716 --> 00:07:14,966
再正常不过了 Penny
That's about as normal as it gets, Penny

92
00:07:15,007 --> 00:07:16,966
那边没什么问题吧?
Everything going alright up there?

93
00:07:17,007 --> 00:07:17,049
没问题 克罗叔叔!

94
00:07:17,091 --> 00:07:18,966
没问题 克罗叔叔!
Just fine, Uncle Qrow!

95
00:07:22,757 --> 00:07:23,924
我又赢了
I win again.

96
00:07:24,466 --> 00:07:26,216
要不我们不玩了?
Maybe we should call it quits?

97
00:07:26,257 --> 00:07:27,132
闭嘴 发牌
Shut up and deal.

98
00:07:30,341 --> 00:07:32,757
你侄女真的是很特别
Your niece sure is one of a kind, huh?

99
00:07:33,424 --> 00:07:34,424
他们都是
They all are.

100
00:07:34,466 --> 00:07:36,424
一起经历了许多
Been through a lot together.

101
00:07:37,632 --> 00:07:39,216
有个可以让他们期待并且给予帮助的人
It's a good thing they had someone

102
00:07:39,257 --> 00:07:41,216
对他们而言是件好事
to look up to and get them through it.

103
00:07:41,882 --> 00:07:43,216
不是所有人都这么幸运
Not everyone is so lucky.

104
00:07:44,799 --> 00:07:46,007
幸运吗 我可不敢说
I don't know about all that.

105
00:07:48,174 --> 00:07:49,799
对了 谢谢
Thanks, by the way.

106
00:07:50,799 --> 00:07:53,424
感谢你和你的队伍给他们的照顾
For looking out for 'em. You and your team.

107
00:07:54,507 --> 00:07:56,341
要是没有下一代的话
What good is saving the world without

108
00:07:56,382 --> 00:07:58,341
拯救世界能有什么好处?
another generation waiting in the wings?

109
00:07:59,007 --> 00:08:00,424
希望他们留给下一代的树不子
Hopefully they'll leave Remnant

110
00:08:00,466 --> 00:08:01,841
要比我们留给他们的要好
better than we left it for them.

111
00:08:04,132 --> 00:08:06,466
要是在以前 我会为这干一杯
Once upon a time, I'd have drank to that.

112
00:08:07,257 --> 00:08:08,882
你知道的 你不应该这么做
You shouldn't do that, you know.

113
00:08:09,382 --> 00:08:10,924
别担心 我已经戒了
Don't worry, I gave that up.

114
00:08:11,091 --> 00:08:13,174
我是指你不该回避他人的称赞
I meant deflect a compliment.

115
00:08:13,632 --> 00:08:15,716
没有你的话 这些孩子也到不了这里
Those kids wouldn't be where they are without you.

116
00:08:16,216 --> 00:08:18,632
你带给他们的影响 比你想象的更大
You've had more of an effect on them than you realize.

117
00:08:20,424 --> 00:08:22,174
呃 克罗叔叔
Uh, Uncle Qrow.

118
00:08:23,007 --> 00:08:24,174
怎么了?
What's going on?

119
00:08:24,216 --> 00:08:24,924
戮兽吗?
Grimm?

120
00:08:25,924 --> 00:08:27,674
不 比这更糟
No. Worse.

121
00:08:28,466 --> 00:08:29,341
你们两个跟着我
You two with me,

122
00:08:29,549 --> 00:08:31,924
Penny 留在车上 盯着点我们的后方
Penny, stay put and keep an eye on our six.

123
00:08:32,716 --> 00:08:34,382
我们可能需要保留点惊喜
We may need an element of surprise.

124
00:08:34,549 --> 00:08:35,216
收到
Affirmative.

125
00:08:35,549 --> 00:08:37,757
我会计划六个可能的结果
I will plan for six possible outcomes.

126
00:08:53,632 --> 00:08:56,174
好了 女士们 让他们看看我们的能耐
Alright ladies, time to show them our teeth.

127
00:09:02,049 --> 00:09:05,799
罗宾!这不是曼特城的大英雄吗
Robyn! Well, if it isn't Mantle's hometown hero.

128
00:09:06,591 --> 00:09:09,924
你阻挡官方军队运输车是有什么原因吗?
Is there a reason you're blocking an official military transport?

129
00:09:10,966 --> 00:09:13,091
克洛弗 真高兴在这里见到你
Clover, I'm so glad you're here.

130
00:09:13,757 --> 00:09:16,216
或许你可以向我解释一下 为什么这辆卡车
Maybe you can help me understand why this truck

131
00:09:16,257 --> 00:09:18,882
本来应该满载着用来维修曼特城
that's supposed to be taking construction materials

132
00:09:18,924 --> 00:09:20,382
外城墙的建筑物资
to fix Mantle's outer wall,

133
00:09:21,132 --> 00:09:23,591
现在却正驶往荒无人烟的地方?
is on its way to the middle of nowhere?

134
00:09:24,216 --> 00:09:25,216
你们迷路了吗?
Are you lost?

135
00:09:25,632 --> 00:09:29,049
苔原上确实很容易找不到路
It's pretty easy to get turned around out here in the tundra,

136
00:09:29,716 --> 00:09:31,049
一切看起来都一个样
everything looks the same.

137
00:09:31,466 --> 00:09:33,049
感谢你的关心
Thanks for checking up on us though.

138
00:09:33,466 --> 00:09:34,716
我们就先上路了
We'll be on our way now.

139
00:09:37,132 --> 00:09:39,257
我本来希望你能跟我直说的
I was hoping you'd play it straight with me.

140
00:09:39,841 --> 00:09:43,216
埃隆伍德在拿阿米特和雪倪尘晶的废弃矿井干什么
What's Ironwood doing with Amity at the old SDC mine?

141
00:09:45,007 --> 00:09:46,174
这个啊
Oh, that.

142
00:09:46,757 --> 00:09:48,466
只是年检而已
Just giving her an annual checkup.

143
00:09:49,341 --> 00:09:52,257
下一届维特节还没那么快到呢
The next Vytal Festival isn't anytime soon,

144
00:09:52,299 --> 00:09:56,966
只有无人机和个别被选定的擎天科学家能过来
only automated drones and a few select Atlas scientists are allowed out here.

145
00:09:57,132 --> 00:10:01,966
而曼特急需的用来抵御戮兽的宝贵资源 正被运到阿米特
And Amity's getting invaluable resources we need in Mantle to protect against Grimm.

146
00:10:03,882 --> 00:10:06,091
看来可不只是检查啊
Seems like more than just a check-up.

147
00:10:08,382 --> 00:10:10,507
你一直在监视我们啊
You've been scoping it out.

148
00:10:11,091 --> 00:10:13,674
没有这些卡车上的补给 我们没法修墙
We can't fix the wall without the supplies on these trucks.

149
00:10:13,924 --> 00:10:16,757
我想曼特的人民应该知道 它们要被用来干什么
I think Mantle deserves to know what they're being used for.

150
00:10:17,632 --> 00:10:21,591
不必如此僵持 告诉我吧
It doesn't have to be difficult. Just tell me.

151
00:10:25,841 --> 00:10:27,716
无可奉告
I'm going to have to pass on that.

152
00:10:30,466 --> 00:10:31,799
那你呢 小矮子?
How 'bout you, pipsqueak?

153
00:10:32,341 --> 00:10:33,341
还有胡子拉碴男
Five o'clock shadow?

154
00:10:33,841 --> 00:10:38,757
你们俩要不要告诉我埃隆伍德有小计划 要使曼特陷入危险?
Either of you want to tell me why Mantle's being put at risk for Ironwood's pet project?

155
00:10:38,799 --> 00:10:40,216
我们是想帮助曼特 我们需要
We're trying to help Mantle, we need -

156
00:10:40,257 --> 00:10:40,966
够了 罗宾
That's enough, Robyn.

157
00:10:42,174 --> 00:10:46,216
作为议员候选人 你应该关注于选举 而不是骚扰猎人
As a potential Councilwoman, you should probably focus on the election instead of harassing Huntsmen.

158
00:10:47,299 --> 00:10:50,007
现在让我们过去
Now, it's time to let us pass.

159
00:10:50,757 --> 00:10:53,007
我觉得你搞错了形势
I think you've misjudged the situation.

160
00:10:53,674 --> 00:10:58,966
无论如何 这些补给都要去它们本来该去的地方: 曼特城
One way or another, these supplies are going to get where they're supposed to go: Mantle.

161
00:10:59,466 --> 00:11:03,216
那我建议你通过议员的合法权力来达成这个目标
Then I suggest you do that through the proper legal channels as a Councilwoman.

162
00:11:03,257 --> 00:11:05,216
如果你能被选上的话
If you get elected.

163
00:11:07,757 --> 00:11:09,924
那样就不好玩了
Now where's the fun in that?

164
00:11:18,257 --> 00:11:19,216
罗宾·修
Robyn Hill.

165
00:11:19,841 --> 00:11:23,716
我想礼貌地请你撤回从车后靠近的猎人们
I would like to politely ask that you call off the Huntresses approaching the rear of the truck.

166
00:11:31,632 --> 00:11:32,174
行吧
Alright.

167
00:11:33,049 --> 00:11:34,591
乔安娜 梅
Joanna, May.

168
00:11:41,799 --> 00:11:43,757
曼特城的守护者哈
The Protector of Mantle, huh?

169
00:11:45,507 --> 00:11:48,216
请让我们过去
Let us through, please.

170
00:12:08,091 --> 00:12:09,174
罗宾
Robyn.

171
00:12:11,757 --> 00:12:12,799
祝你选举好运
Good luck at the election.

172
00:12:21,507 --> 00:12:22,757
真是好险
That was a close one.

173
00:12:22,799 --> 00:12:24,007
要你说
You're telling me.

174
00:12:28,257 --> 00:12:28,924
现在怎么做?
What now?

175
00:12:29,632 --> 00:12:33,591
我想知道为什么阿米特竞技场突然变得那么重要
I want to know why Amity Colosseum is suddenly so important.

176
00:12:34,216 --> 00:12:36,174
不惜一切代价
Whatever it takes.

177
00:12:56,382 --> 00:13:00,299
你的技艺仍然有那些糟糕又不精炼的瑕疵
Your technique still has those maddening sloppy touches.

178
00:13:00,882 --> 00:13:03,382
但你已经学会了如何让它们为你所用
But you've learned how to make them work for you.

179
00:13:04,049 --> 00:13:05,382
你已经与它们融为一体了
You've made them your own.

180
00:13:05,799 --> 00:13:08,757
哇 这可几乎是夸奖了
Wow, that was very close to a compliment.

181
00:13:08,799 --> 00:13:10,716
我可没往那想
I didn't intend it that way.

182
00:13:10,924 --> 00:13:12,424
大概我们都会犯错吧
We all make mistakes, I guess.

183
00:13:16,466 --> 00:13:18,424
你也成长了些嘛
You've grown up a bit, haven't you?

184
00:13:19,174 --> 00:13:21,882
你不再是那个紧攥着家名的小女孩了
You're not the little girl clinging to the family name anymore.

185
00:13:22,716 --> 00:13:25,507
自从信标陷落后 我也没那机会
Since Beacon, I haven't really had a choice.

186
00:13:25,966 --> 00:13:29,424
父亲的世界观不再和我的一致了
Father's view of the world no longer matches with mine.

187
00:13:30,007 --> 00:13:32,674
无论如何 我很高兴你迈出了脚步
Whatever the case, I am glad to see you've moved on.

188
00:13:33,257 --> 00:13:37,674
把自己和雪倪的家名隔离开 是我做过的最有益的事情
Distancing myself from the Schnee name is the most beneficial thing I've ever done.

189
00:13:38,091 --> 00:13:41,466
我们能一起前行 不受他的影响
We can move forward without him, together.

190
00:13:42,216 --> 00:13:44,632
埃隆伍德将军手下会有你的容身之处的
I know General Ironwood would have a place for you.

191
00:13:46,799 --> 00:13:51,841
他愿意接纳我的话 我会很感激 但我恐怕不会接受那份邀请
I would be grateful to him if he did, but I'm not sure I could accept.

192
00:13:53,507 --> 00:13:54,257
真的?
Really?

193
00:13:54,674 --> 00:13:55,799
只是...
It's just.

194
00:13:56,549 --> 00:13:59,091
我们的王国不应是这样子的
Our kingdom isn't supposed to be like this.

195
00:13:59,132 --> 00:14:01,091
恐惧而隔离
Fearful, and withdrawn.

196
00:14:01,424 --> 00:14:05,424
我们应该打开国境帮助世界 而不是封闭起来
We should be opening our borders to help the world, not closing them down.

197
00:14:05,466 --> 00:14:06,466
我们会的
We will, though.

198
00:14:06,716 --> 00:14:08,924
只要我们度过了这次风暴一我们会的
Once we've weathered the storm, we will.

199
00:14:10,632 --> 00:14:15,882
我知道将军并不完美 但他是在做他认为对的事
I know the General hasn't done everything perfectly, but he's doing what he thinks is right.

200
00:14:17,632 --> 00:14:20,216
每个人都觉得自己做的事是对的
Everybody thinks what they're doing is right,

201
00:14:20,966 --> 00:14:25,966
但通常他们也只是为自己和他们的秘密着想
but usually, they're just looking out for themselves, and their secrets.

202
00:14:26,007 --> 00:14:28,132
埃隆伍德没有隐藏秘密
Ironwood isn't keeping secrets.

203
00:14:28,924 --> 00:14:29,716
至少没有对我隐藏
Not from me.

204
00:14:31,924 --> 00:14:33,424
你确定吗
Can you be sure?

205
00:14:40,882 --> 00:14:41,841
跟我来
Come with me.

206
00:14:42,341 --> 00:14:44,174
我有东西要给你看
There's something I want to show you.

207
00:15:44,591 --> 00:15:47,007
下午好 今天感觉如何?
Good afternoon, feeling better today?

208
00:15:47,632 --> 00:15:48,341
早上好
Good morning.

209
00:15:49,382 --> 00:15:51,132
你想来点茶吗?
Would you care for some tea?

210
00:15:51,174 --> 00:15:55,716
我确实想在冷天喝些热茶
I do like hot tea on a cold day.

211
00:15:56,507 --> 00:15:59,216
会让我想起家
Reminds me of home.

212
00:16:03,049 --> 00:16:05,841
外面冷吗
Is it cold outside?

213
00:16:07,382 --> 00:16:08,841
是的 亲爱的
Yes, dear.

214
00:16:11,132 --> 00:16:12,882
那就是冬之少女
That's the Winter Maiden.

215
00:16:14,841 --> 00:16:16,466
她随时都可能离世
She could pass any day now.

216
00:16:17,924 --> 00:16:21,966
直到那一刻发生 我是芙莉雅唯一能见的人
Until that happens, I'm the only person Fria's allowed to see.

217
00:16:25,299 --> 00:16:28,716
埃隆伍德已经决定让你来当下一任...
Ironwood's chosen you to be the next...

218
00:16:29,507 --> 00:16:31,674
等她死了
W- When she dies.

219
00:16:33,216 --> 00:16:34,966
你知道这事多久了
How long have you known?

220
00:16:35,216 --> 00:16:36,507
自从信标陷落
Since Beacon fell.

221
00:16:37,174 --> 00:16:38,507
这不会让你不安吗
Doesn't it bother you?

222
00:16:38,799 --> 00:16:41,257
他可以说是安排了你的整个军事生涯啊
He practically groomed your whole military career.

223
00:16:42,049 --> 00:16:46,091
当将军第一次向我提这件事 我的确觉得不舒服
It did at first, when the General first proposed it to me.

224
00:16:47,299 --> 00:16:51,257
但我越想 就越觉得这是我的光荣
But the more I thought about it, the more saw it as a privilege,

225
00:16:51,924 --> 00:16:56,466
一个为擎天 为树不子奉献的机会
a chance to do some real good for Atlas. For Remnant.

226
00:16:57,007 --> 00:17:00,382
但你的命运就这样被决定了 不受你的左右
But your destiny was chosen for you, without your input.

227
00:17:00,591 --> 00:17:04,216
也许吧 但这是我自己选的
Perhaps, but I'm choosing it now.

228
00:17:04,841 --> 00:17:05,924
我让它变成了我的命运
I've made it my own.

229
00:17:06,507 --> 00:17:08,549
我为此非常自豪
And I take great pride in it.

230
00:17:09,007 --> 00:17:11,924
这与父亲或将军都无关
That has nothing to do with Father, or the General.

231
00:17:12,674 --> 00:17:14,257
这是我的
That belongs to me

232
00:17:17,091 --> 00:17:19,716
我猜 这件事我们必定都做过
I guess we've both had to do a little bit of that.

233
00:17:20,674 --> 00:17:22,007
开拓属于自己的路
Carving out our own way.

234
00:17:24,341 --> 00:17:25,674
确实
I suppose we have.

235
00:17:30,382 --> 00:17:32,174
说到家名
Speaking of the family name.

236
00:17:32,674 --> 00:17:33,924
他在干什么
What is he doing?

237
00:17:34,257 --> 00:17:35,966
如果我竞选成功
If I'm elected Councilman,

238
00:17:45,966 --> 00:17:49,549
这些措施不仅鲁莽 而且是罪行
It is my belief that these measures are not only reckless, but criminal.

239
00:17:50,216 --> 00:17:56,049
因为货物无法进出擎天 我知道你们很多人在受苦
With no shipments allowed to enter or leave the kingdom, I know many are suffering.

240
00:17:56,216 --> 00:18:00,716
而我的家庭正在和你们经历共同的风雨
And my family has been weathering the same storm as many of you.

241
00:18:02,091 --> 00:18:08,424
这一决定立即生效 我被迫关闭一场雪倪尘晶的外围产业
Effective immediately, Iam forced to shut downall nonessential SDCoperations.

242
00:18:10,924 --> 00:18:17,591
如果我当选议员 我会做出必要的改变来弥补埃隆伍德造成的破坏
If elected to office, I will make the changes necessary to fix what Ironwood has broken.

243
00:18:18,424 --> 00:18:21,091
我希望你们投票前问问自己
I hope you ask yourself before the vote,

244
00:18:21,841 --> 00:18:25,591
你还能信任谁来阻止埃隆伍德?
"Can you trust anyone else to stop Ironwood?"

245
00:18:26,049 --> 00:18:29,049
罗宾·修能让你找回工作吗?
Will Robyn Hill be able to get your jobs back?

246
00:18:37,632 --> 00:18:45,882
我想... 就在刚才 父亲点着了能引燃整个王国的火花
I think... I think Father may have just provided the spark that's going to set this kingdom on fire.